# NAZURI COLLECTIONS
## Project Vision, Brand Strategy & Website Requirements

**Project:** Nazuri Collections Showcase Website  
**Document:** 01 – Project Vision & Requirements  
**Status:** Approved foundation for development  
**Brand tagline:** Premium Abayas and Gowns in Town  
**Established:** Since 2023

---

# 1. Project Overview

Nazuri Collections is a women's fashion brand specializing in elegant, premium and contemporary modest fashion, particularly abayas, gowns and dresses.

The purpose of this project is to build a modern, visually appealing and professional online fashion showcase that communicates the brand's identity, displays its fashion collections and encourages potential customers to make inquiries.

The website must create a premium shopping experience without implementing a complicated e-commerce infrastructure.

It should feel like visiting a well-organized luxury fashion boutique.

# 2. Project Vision

Build a distinctive digital presence for Nazuri Collections that:

- Creates a strong and recognizable brand identity.
- Presents fashion products through high-quality visual experiences.
- Makes product discovery simple and enjoyable.
- Builds customer confidence and brand credibility.
- Encourages inquiries through WhatsApp and social media.
- Provides an excellent experience on mobile phones, tablets and desktops.

The website should be visually competitive with contemporary premium fashion boutiques.

# 3. Target Audience

The primary audience consists of women interested in:

- Elegant abayas.
- Modern modest fashion.
- Premium gowns.
- Stylish dresses.
- Two-piece outfits.
- Special occasion outfits.

The interface should appeal to customers who value elegance, quality, simplicity and presentation.

# 4. Brand Identity and Visual Direction

## 4.1 Brand Personality

Nazuri Collections should communicate:

- Elegance.
- Sophistication.
- Confidence.
- Femininity.
- Exclusivity.
- Quality.
- Modern fashion.

Avoid a cheap-looking, crowded or overly decorative interface.

## 4.2 Design Inspiration

Use the visual principles of premium fashion brands such as Zara and COS as inspiration.

Do not copy their websites, layouts, assets or branding.

Develop a unique Nazuri Collections identity.

## 4.3 Color Palette

Use the following initial brand palette:

| Color | Hex | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Charcoal | #1F2328 | Primary dark surfaces and text |
| Off-white | #F5F5F5 | Main backgrounds |
| Silver Grey | #B5B5B5 | Secondary elements |
| Champagne Gold | #C9A66B | Accents and highlights |
| White | #FFFFFF | Clean content surfaces |

Gold should be used selectively for active navigation, subtle highlights and important details.

Do not overuse gold gradients, shadows or decorative borders.

## 4.4 Typography

Use an elegant, readable typographic system.

Recommended direction:

- Elegant serif typography for selected headings.
- Modern sans-serif typography for body text and navigation.
- Clear visual hierarchy.
- Consistent font weights and spacing.
- Comfortable readability on mobile devices.

Typography must enhance the fashion imagery rather than compete with it.

# 5. Website Structure and Pages

The website should contain the following main pages.

## 5.1 Home Page

The homepage is the most important brand presentation page.

It should include:

1. Elegant announcement or promotional area, only when relevant.
2. Responsive navigation.
3. Strong hero section with compelling fashion photography.
4. Clear brand introduction.
5. Featured collections.
6. Selected product highlights.
7. Brand introduction or About preview.
8. Customer inquiry call-to-action.
9. Instagram/social media discovery section where suitable.
10. Professional footer.

The hero section must communicate the brand's identity immediately.

Avoid excessive text and unnecessary sections.

## 5.2 Abayas Page

A dedicated collection page for abayas.

Requirements:

- Attractive collection introduction.
- Well-organized product grid.
- Consistent image presentation.
- Product names.
- Available colors where supplied.
- Product descriptions where supplied.
- Optional category filtering and sorting if useful.
- Clear product inquiry actions.

## 5.3 Magauni / Gowns Page

A dedicated collection page for gowns and dresses.

Requirements:

- Distinctive collection presentation.
- High-quality product photography.
- Consistent product cards.
- Product information.
- Available color variations where applicable.
- WhatsApp inquiry action.

## 5.4 Product Details

Where appropriate, provide an individual product detail experience.

It may include:

- Larger product photography.
- Product name.
- Product description.
- Available colors.
- Other supplied product information.
- WhatsApp inquiry action.

Product detail functionality must not become a shopping cart or checkout system.

## 5.5 About Us Page

Explain the Nazuri Collections brand story.

Communicate:

- Who Nazuri Collections is.
- Its fashion identity.
- Its commitment to elegant fashion presentation.
- Its journey since 2023, where applicable.
- Its customer-oriented approach.

Do not invent company history, achievements, addresses or business claims.

## 5.6 Contact Page

Provide convenient ways to contact the brand.

Include:

- WhatsApp contact.
- Instagram.
- TikTok.
- Other verified contact information when provided.

Contact details must be configurable.

Never invent a WhatsApp number or social media account.

Use clear placeholders until genuine contact information is supplied.

# 6. Product Presentation Requirements

Product photography is a major part of this website.

The product showcase must:

- Preserve the original appearance of supplied garments.
- Avoid stretching or distorting images.
- Use consistent image ratios where appropriate.
- Provide suitable image cropping.
- Maintain good image quality.
- Support different product colors and variations.
- Display products in an organized and attractive way.

Use product photographs supplied by the project owner.

Do not download or substitute random product images from the internet.

Do not alter the actual garment design when processing product images.

# 7. User Experience Requirements

The website must provide:

- Intuitive navigation.
- Clear visual hierarchy.
- Consistent spacing.
- Responsive product grids.
- Easy-to-understand buttons.
- Smooth but restrained interactions.
- Useful hover effects.
- Accessible navigation.
- Clear loading and empty states where applicable.
- Helpful feedback for interactive elements.

Mobile users must receive the same quality of experience as desktop users.

# 8. Responsive Design

Support:

- Small mobile devices.
- Large mobile devices.
- Tablets.
- Laptops.
- Desktop screens.

The mobile experience must include:

- An elegant mobile navigation menu.
- Readable typography.
- Properly sized buttons.
- Appropriate product grid columns.
- Images that fit the viewport.
- No horizontal overflow.
- Touch-friendly controls.

# 9. Conversion and Customer Engagement

The primary conversion goal is to encourage customers to contact Nazuri Collections.

Implement:

- WhatsApp inquiry links.
- Clear collection navigation.
- Product-specific inquiry actions.
- Social media links.
- Contact calls-to-action.

WhatsApp links must use a configurable placeholder until the official number is supplied.

The website should not falsely imply that an order, payment or reservation has been completed.

# 10. Performance and Trust

The website should:

- Load quickly.
- Use optimized local images.
- Avoid unnecessary animations.
- Avoid unnecessary external dependencies.
- Present consistent and accurate information.
- Have functional navigation and links.
- Display a professional brand identity.

# 11. Scope and Limitations

This is a lightweight website showcase, not a full e-commerce platform.

The following are outside the current project scope:

- Backend server.
- Database.
- Customer registration and authentication.
- Shopping cart.
- Online checkout.
- Payment gateway.
- Order management system.
- Inventory management system.
- Admin dashboard.

Do not introduce these systems without explicit approval.

# 12. Definition of Success

The project will be considered successful when:

1. The website communicates a distinctive premium fashion identity.
2. Visitors can easily discover different collections.
3. Product images are displayed professionally.
4. All navigation and interactive elements work.
5. The website performs well on mobile and desktop.
6. Customers can easily contact the business.
7. The website is accessible online through a reliable hosting solution.
8. The codebase remains lightweight and maintainable.

---

**Final Direction**

Nazuri Collections must look and feel like a modern premium fashion boutique, not a generic product listing website.

Every design and development decision must support elegance, clarity, product presentation, usability and customer engagement.